                                                                                                              
    If it passes those checks                                                                                 
                                                                                                              
    You have a clean path:                                                                                    
                                                                                                              
    The Win 11 laptop → fresh USB stick → deliver work                                                        
                                                                                                              
    Specifically:                                                                                             
                                                                                                              
    1. Get a brand-new USB stick today if possible. From a store you've used before, paid cash if you can,    
    packaging sealed. (Old USB sticks are vectors — they can have reprogrammed firmware.)                     
    2. On the Win 11 laptop, download a fresh ISO of whatever Linux distro you want (Ubuntu, MX, Debian)      
    from the official site. Verify the SHA-256 if you can — but the public website is fine, the               
    attacker isn't likely to have compromised Ubuntu.com.                                                     
