    weird.                                                                                                    
    9. Deliver through a fresh channel — new email address from the Win 11 laptop, used once, then            
    abandoned. Or whatever the client uses (SFTP, GitHub, etc., but with new credentials created on the Win   
    11 machine).                                                                                              
                                                                                                              
    Why this works                                                                                            
                                                                                                              
    • The fresh USB boots a clean kernel that hasn't been touched                                             
    • Read-only mount means even if the drive has a malicious firmware, the booted OS can't be tricked        
    • The Win 11 laptop has its own BIOS, not shared with your compromised machines (presumably)              
    • Cellular tethering skips your home network where the attacker might be observing                        
                                                                                                              
    What to do with the high school laptop first                                                              
                                                                                                              
    Before you trust it with anything:                                                                        
                                                                                                              
